.TH scanr-output-events 1  "scanr-output-events " 
.SH NAME
scanr\-output\-events \- Write the raw JSONL event stream, decompressing it if needed
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBscanr\-output\-events\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write the raw JSONL event stream, decompressing it if needed
.PP
This is the file verbatim. With spans on, most probes are represented by a `probe_span` rather than a `probe_result`, so filtering these events for `probe_result` does not give you every result — `scanr output results` does.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>

